      "q": "If $y = \\sin x + \\cos x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$.",
      "options": [
        "$\\cos x + \\sin x$",
        "$\\cos x - \\sin x$",
        "$-\\cos x - \\sin x$",
        "$-\\cos x + \\sin x$"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explain": "The derivative of $\\sin x$ is $\\cos x$, and the derivative of $\\cos x$ is $-\\sin x$. Therefore, $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\cos x - \\sin x$.",
